    "meaning": {
      "story": "This song depicts a dangerous role reversal where the protagonist, once pursued with playful indifference by an unsure partner who said 'maybe,' finds themselves hunted after setting boundaries. The narrative shifts from confident banter to ominous warning as the pursuer's obsession reveals they possess intimate secrets about the singer's home and family. Ultimately, it is a cautionary tale about how hesitation can curdle into stalking behavior, turning a simple rejection into an inescapable nightmare.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "name": "Chorus",
          "interpretation": "The core conflict establishes the power dynamic flip where 'maybe' transforms from polite uncertainty to relentless harassment disguised as affectionate nicknames.",
          "keyLine": "\"Now you can't stop callin' me baby\""
        },
        {
          "name": "Verse 1",
          "interpretation": "The singer contrasts their past vulnerability with current confidence, noting how the other person's energy has darkened as they realize they have lost control.",
